  #line-at(62.16pt, 486.84pt, ". The dead layers consist of defects, dislocations, vacancies and have a low dielectric constant. As the ")
  #line-at(54pt, 507.48pt, "thickness of STO membrane increases, the percentage contribution of the dead layers reduces therefore a ")
  #line-at(54pt, 528.24pt, "higher dielectric constant is observed. On the other hand, the k-value stays in the lower range (115~140) ")
  #line-at(54pt, 548.88pt, "in 100 μm contact pads compared to 50μm pads (150~186) in the 200 nm membrane.  The 50 nm ")
  #line-at(54pt, 569.64pt, "nanomembrane had similar trends as well, the range of k was 50~60 in 100 μm contact pads whereas it ")
  #line-at(54pt, 590.28pt, "was 70~82 in 50 μm pads. The origin of this trend is not clearly understood however it may be ")
  #line-at(54pt, 611.04pt, "hypothesized that, bigger contact pads might have damaged the STO membrane a bit more compared to ")
  #line-at(54pt, 631.68pt, "smaller ones during metal deposition or nanomembrane transfer process leading to lower crystallinity and ")
  #line-at(54pt, 652.44pt, "degradation of the dielectric constant.  One more trend was observed, the value of k was slightly higher ")
  #line-at(54pt, 673.08pt, "after annealing, the k-value was 105~160 and 31~38 in 200 nm and 50 nm STO membrane respectively ")
  #line-at(54pt, 693.72pt, "before annealing. A possible reason for improved k after annealing was that the annealing process might ")
  #line-at(54pt, 714.48pt, "have healed some damages of the membrane that occurred during metal deposition or transfer process. ")
]

