#original-page(612pt, 792pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 11.977pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(303pt, 739.56pt, "5 ")
  #line-at(54pt, 65.16pt, "Different annealing temperatures and ambient conditions might play a crucial role in the damage recovery ")
  #line-at(54pt, 85.8pt, "process and facilitate more optimization of the membrane quality and the dielectric constant. Our future ")
  #line-at(54pt, 106.56pt, "studies are anticipated to focus on this optimization and contain the relevant results.  ")
  #line-at(72pt, 127.2pt, "In conclusion, 200 nm and 500 nm single-crystalline STO nanomembranes (confirmed by XRD ")
  #line-at(54pt, 147.96pt, "measurements) were transferred on GaN for potential applications as gate-dielectric (transistors) and field ")
  #line-at(54pt, 168.6pt, "dielectric (transistors and diodes). The detailed electrical properties of the membrane were reported such ")
  #line-at(54pt, 189.36pt, "as leakage current, capacitance-voltage, frequency dispersion, dielectric constant and its dependance on ")
  #line-at(54pt, 210pt, "membrane thickness, contact pad size and annealing. A simple analytic-numeric method was introduced ")
  #line-at(54pt, 230.76pt, "to evaluate the dielectric constant of a thin film. The transferred nano-membrane had negligible leakage ")
  #line-at(54pt, 251.4pt, "current up to 6 V and 11 V for 50 nm and 200 nm thick STO membrane respectively. There was almost ")
  #line-at(54pt, 272.16pt, "no frequency dispersion in the C-V profile in the range of 10 kHz- 500 kHz, and the value of the ")
  #line-at(54pt, 292.8pt, "capacitance scaled proportionally with contact area- indicating a high-quality dielectric. The measured ")
  #line-at(54pt, 313.56pt, "dielectric constant in 50 nm and 200 nm STO membrane was 50~82 and 115~186  respectively. It was ")
  #line-at(54pt, 334.2pt, "found that smaller pad size and higher thickness of the membrane favor higher dielectric constant and the ")
  #line-at(54pt, 354.96pt, "possible physical reason behind this was explained.  ")
  #line-at(54pt, 389.64pt, "We gratefully acknowledge the support by NSF (National Science Foundation) through MRSEC ")
  #line-at(54pt, 403.44pt, "(Materials Research Science and Engineering Center), University of Wisconsin-Madison, program: ")
